.nf
YASMV manual                                                 workspace

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
workspace open "<directory>"
workspace show
workspace clear

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Choose the directory used to store model revisions, named expressions, jobs,
traces, and scenarios. The default is .yasmv-workbench in the current directory.
Python 3.10 or newer is required.

open creates or opens the directory. Wait for active jobs to finish before
switching directories. A directory can have only one owner: close any other
CLI or HTTP service using it first.

show reports the directory, loaded native model, selected native trace, and
saved revision, job, and scenario selections.

clear permanently deletes the workspace's saved revisions (including goals,
properties, watches, and scenario mappings), jobs and their evidence, traces,
and scenarios. It also resets saved selections and closes compiled sessions.
It keeps the workspace directory and ownership lock, unrelated files at its
root, and the native loaded model, input bindings, and traces. Exported files
outside the managed artifact directories are preserved.

Clear requires no active jobs. Use job cancel followed by job wait, or let
jobs finish, before clearing. Repeated clears of an empty workspace are valid.
There is no confirmation prompt. workspace show and artifact listings do not
recreate deleted artifacts. The next model-dependent workspace command saves
a fresh revision of the loaded model; a native trace is replayed when reused.

Opening a workspace preserves the native model and trace selection. Use
read-model to load a model. The existing one-model-load-attempt rule applies;
start a new yasmv process to load another model.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> workspace open "./investigation"
>> workspace show
>> workspace clear

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help read-model, help goal, help property, help watch, help job, help scenario.
